#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166420 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d13b0d31-65b8-550f-b97b-f4ece63bf834" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "22a44ff4-55e7-51db-a54e-26ef23764fa4" :question/math-academy-id "e-12490" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)$ and the region $D$ given by\n\n$f(x,y) =\\dfrac{xy}2, \\qquad D = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2y, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 4 \\big\\}$.\n\nAccording to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b) \\in D$ such that the volume of the solid enclosed between the surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane over the region $D$ equals the volume of the right cylinder with base $D$ and height $f(a,b)$. Find $a$ given that $b=2$." :question/worked-solution "According to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b) \\in D$ such that\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_D f(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A = f(a,b) \\cdot \\textrm{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral on the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)f(x, y)dA &= ∬_(D)\\frac{xy}{2}dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{4}∫_{0}^{2y}\\frac{xy}{2}dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{4}[\\frac{x^{2}y}{4}]_{x = 0}^{x = 2y}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{4}y^{3}dy \\\\\n&= [\\frac{y^{4}}{4}]_{y = 0}^{y = 4} \\\\\n&= 64\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nArea(D) &= ∬_(D)dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{4}∫_{0}^{2y}dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{4}[x]_{x = 0}^{x = 2y}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{4}2ydy \\\\\n&= [y^{2}]_{y = 0}^{y = 4} \\\\\n&= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we are told that $b=2$. So, our initial equation simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n64 &= f(a, 2) \\cdot 16 \\\\\n64 &= \\frac{a \\cdot 2}{2} \\cdot 16 \\\\\n64 &= 16a \\\\\na &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\left(4,2 \\right) \\in D\n$$\n\nTherefore, the answer is $a = 4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166421 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b43eea5b-9da3-5fe0-a28c-cc01aed3627a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "0a06a8ae-69d6-5ded-979e-149f650a1676" :question/math-academy-id "e-12491" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y) = xy$ on the region $D = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: -1 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: x \\leq y \\leq 3x \\big\\}$ given that the area of the region is $3$ square units." :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{ave} &= (1)/(Area(D))∬_(D)f(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}∬_(D)xydA \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}∫_{-1}^{2}∫_{x}^{3x}xydydx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}∫_{-1}^{2}[\\frac{xy^{2}}{2}]_{y = x}^{y = 3x}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}∫_{-1}^{2}4x^{3}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}[x^{4}]_{x =-1}^{x = 2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}(16 - 1) \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166422 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4e5deee-e910-5bb1-9d9a-0b24886ab6c1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Polar Region"}] :question/id #uuid "13800660-08b4-50af-93b4-1013bbf41e66" :question/math-academy-id "e-12492" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y) = 15xy^2$ on the portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at the origin, where $x\\geq 0$, and $y \\leq 0$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region $D$:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3147/Source/Images/810ee225582208f31ff49948545b0349.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Area}(D) = \\dfrac{1}{4} \\cdot \\pi \\cdot 1^2 = \\dfrac\\pi 4\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_{\\textrm{ave}} = \\dfrac{1}{\\textrm{Area}(D)} \\, \\iint\\limits_D f(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} f(x,y) \\ \\mathrm d A = \\iint\\limits_{\\Delta} \\ f(r\\cos\\theta, r\\sin\\theta) \\: r \\ \\mathrm d r \\mathrm d \\theta\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r, \\theta)$, the region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta = \\left\\{(r,\\theta) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq r \\leq 1, \\: \\dfrac{3\\pi}{2} \\leq \\theta \\leq 2\\pi\\right\\}\n$$\n\nUsing the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)15xy^{2}dA &= ∬_(Δ)15r\\cos θ \\cdot (r\\sin θ)^{2}rdrdθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{3π/2}^{2π}∫_{0}^{1}15r^{4}\\cos θ\\sin^{2} θdrdθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{3π/2}^{2π}3\\cos θ\\sin^{2} θ∫_{0}^{1}5r^{4}drdθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{3π/2}^{2π}3\\cos θ\\sin^{2} θ[r^{5}]_{0}^{1}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{3π/2}^{2π}3\\cos θ\\sin^{2} θ(1^{5} - 0)dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{3π/2}^{2π}3\\cos θ\\sin^{2} θdθ \\\\\n&= [\\sin^{3} θ]_{3π/2}^{2π} \\\\\n&= (\\sin^{3} (2π) - \\sin^{3} (\\frac{3π}{2})) \\\\\n&= (0 - (-1)) \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf_{\\textrm{ave}} = \\dfrac{4}{\\pi} \\cdot 1 = \\dfrac{4}{\\pi}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d13b0d31-65b8-550f-b97b-f4ece63bf834" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc8f709f-dbc0-5961-a020-845351fe1b5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163839} {:answer/id #uuid "d94ba300-2a81-571b-8829-4ba34cc4e402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163840} {:answer/id #uuid "ec0449a8-ed59-5145-afd6-ca6c198fd73b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163841} {:answer/id #uuid "fb0fe76c-e469-55e5-bf04-44c4f1c78766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163842} {:answer/id #uuid "6819f32c-c237-56ea-ba36-f9df65a4cada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6819f32c-c237-56ea-ba36-f9df65a4cada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163843} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a33be06-25c9-5987-ad05-781aa4edc8f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163838}] :question/id #uuid "185b68b4-cdef-58dd-9006-867ebfafd06d" :question/math-academy-id "q-163059" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x, y)$ and the region $D$ given by\n\n$f(x, y) = x^{2} + 2y + 1, D = {(x, y): 0 \\le x \\le 2, 0 \\le y \\le 3}$.\n\nAccording to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a, b) ∈ D$ such that the volume of the solid enclosed between the surface $z = f(x, y)$ and the $xy$-plane over the region $D$ equals the volume of the right cylinder with base $D$ and height $f(a, b)$. Find $b$ given that $a = 1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167072 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b43eea5b-9da3-5fe0-a28c-cc01aed3627a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e4db2d2-6edd-5e92-83a0-a0059d87eca0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{80}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163851} {:answer/id #uuid "5839e7ae-ad3b-579b-a1f7-4098c74b07bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163852} {:answer/id #uuid "66393c67-fd69-5788-b90d-60e15759e154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163853} {:answer/id #uuid "6b5e6964-aa60-5d9e-a5b1-552be32b20e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163854} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1ceae8-ef8a-5865-adcb-52e7e0b93c02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{42}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e4db2d2-6edd-5e92-83a0-a0059d87eca0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{80}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163851} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ca3adf5-bf4a-5cb1-ae21-1c842c137a57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163850}] :question/id #uuid "b5fbae5f-d41d-5595-bcf0-ce1fbfd9706b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163063" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x, y) = x^{2} - 4y^{3}$ on the region $D = {(x, y): 0 \\le x \\le 1, 0 \\le y \\le 3}$."}]}
